# MagicTime scheduler series
#
# The patches are generated against the exact AOSP16 commit and are applied
# in this order by ../apply-scheduler-patches.sh.
#
# 0001-walt-eevdf-cass-core.patch
#   Net-adapted scheduler closure from the common ancestor
#   a28b116d7545dd4d5c4b52becfcb803bb135c243 through MagicTime
#   eba8dbd9d11b479cae68918826c344065a6b5d3c. It includes the WALT removal,
#   EEVDF data model/selection, CASS, PELT/uclamp and the final rbtree fix.
#
# 0002-aosp-abi-thermal-platform.patch
#   AOSP16-specific platform/vendor closure: cpufreq/thermal pressure,
#   binder/proc/RMNET callers and the small ABI adaptations required to keep
#   AOSP16 task_struct/cgroup and mm lifetime semantics.
#
# 0003-aosp16-core-api-bridge.patch
#   Bridges scheduler-core calls to the older AOSP16 migration, cpuset,
#   rcuwait, workqueue, cpuidle and smp-call APIs found by the first CI build.
#
# 0004-aosp16-aux-api-bridge.patch
#   Bridges softirq accounting, cpumask iteration and the AOSP16 energy-model
#   API reported by the next CI build.
#
# 0005-aosp16-rbtree-waitqueue-bridge.patch
#   Supplies the cached-rbtree insertion helper and maps the newer waitqueue,
#   kthread and cpuset-DL hooks to their AOSP16 equivalents.
#
# 0006-aosp16-rbtree-erase-bridge.patch
#   Accounts for AOSP16's void rb_erase_cached() return convention.
#
# 0007-aosp16-topology-irqwork-bridge.patch
#   Maps the newer energy-model state query and hard irq_work initializer to
#   their AOSP16 equivalents.
#
# 0008-aosp16-psi-membarrier-bridge.patch
#   Restores AOSP16's standard PSI implementation (the MagicTime RT polling
#   PSI variant is outside this port) and declares its RCU-safe task helper.
#
# 0009-aosp16-psi-memstall-flag.patch
#   Restores the AOSP16 PF_MEMSTALL task flag required by the standard PSI
#   memstall accounting path.
#
# 0010-aosp16-task-abi-bridge.patch
#   Adds source-compatible task state/cpumask aliases and the AOSP16 fault
#   signal helper while retaining the MagicTime scheduler field names.
#
# 0011-aosp16-scheduler-annotation-bridge.patch
#   Restores the AOSP16 RCU-trace task bit and resched annotation hook used
#   by the unchanged architecture and BPF code.
#
# 0012-aosp16-cgroup-rbtree-proc-bridge.patch
#   Aligns cpuset attach, interval-tree callbacks and procfs with the AOSP16
#   interfaces after removing the WALT/schedtune surface.
#
# 0013-aosp16-rtree-prio-bridge.patch
#   Restores MAX_USER_RT_PRIO and uses the matching augmented-rbtree callback
#   form in the AOSP16 VMA code.
#
# 0014-aosp16-rcu-vmalloc-bridge.patch
#   Renames the RCU expedited-quiescent bit and uses the matching vmalloc
#   augmented-rbtree callback form.
#
# 0015-aosp16-nhz-load-bridge.patch
#   Removes the newer cpu_load_update_nohz hooks; AOSP16 uses the existing
#   calc_load_nohz start/stop accounting pair in the tick path.
#
# 0016-aosp16-rt-walt-sysfs-bridge.patch
#   Restores cpupri's RT query for softirq deferral and removes the orphaned
#   WALT sched_load_boost sysfs attribute.
#
# 0017-aosp16-runtime-walt-bridge.patch
#   Removes the remaining sched_set_boost coupling from cpu-boost while
#   retaining its input-frequency boost path.
#
# 0018-aosp16-sysctl-bridge.patch
#   Removes orphaned scheduler sysctl entries whose AOSP16 variables were not
#   present in the ported scheduler.
#
# 0019-aosp16-irq-work-smp-bridge.patch
#   Shares IRQ-work flag definitions with AOSP16 smp_types.h to avoid duplicate
#   enum declarations when both headers are included.
#
# The patches intentionally do not change the stable workflow or defconfig.
# The experimental fragment is appended only by the manual workflow.
